    "title": "Robert Stone Reacts To Interim WWE NXT General Manager Role - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Thomas Lowson ,\n40 minutes ago\nRobert Stone will be laying down the law in WWE NXT after being appointed the Interim General Manager of the brand by Shawn Michaels.\nMichaels and Stone were part of a segment during the latest episode of WWE NXT and neither mentioned former GM Ava by name.\nOn Twitter, Stone reacted to his new role, pointing out that he will also remain in his current role with the WWE Evolve brand.\nFormer NXT GM Ava shared on social media last week that she was leaving WWE after choosing not to re-sign with the promotion.\nAva, the daughter of The Rock, had been with the company since 2020 and had spent much of her career as the on-screen authority figure.",
    "summary": "Robert Stone will be laying down the law in WWE NXT after being appointed the Interim General Manager of the brand by Shawn Michaels. Michaels and Stone were part of a segment during the latest episode of WWE NXT and neither mentioned former GM Ava by name. On Twitter, Stone reacted to his new role, pointing out that he will also remain in his current role with the WWE Evolve brand. Former NXT GM Ava shared on social media last week that she was leaving WWE after choosing not to re-sign with the promotion.",
